        },
        "rationale": "Building an n8n-style template doesn't need a new script-execution engine designed from scratch for the in-browser case — that infrastructure is already real and load-bearing elsewhere in the app.",
        "evidence": "See the How a Script Actually Runs mechanism and the cited sources.",
        "caveats": "This only resolves the client-side half of the question. It says nothing about whether a trigger can fire when nobody has the tab open — see the second concept.",
        "documentation": "See the How a Script Actually Runs mechanism."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "graph-application-template-catalog-mechanism",
      "type": "topic-mechanism",
      "label": "How a Script Actually Runs",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -1800,
        "y": 1360
      },
      "width": 400,
      "height": 280,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": false,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "How a Script Actually Runs",
        "mechanism": "A script node's text runs inside a sandboxed iframe, isolated from the host page. It talks back to the host exclusively through postMessage RPC calls, each carrying a per-run token so the host can distinguish and rate-limit calls from a specific run.",
        "conditions": "The graph must be open in a live browser tab; the script node must have allowMutations enabled for its RPC calls to actually persist changes (dryRun otherwise).",
        "definitionKey": "topic-mechanism",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "topic-mechanism",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-mechanism.node-class.node",
          "defaults": {
            "label": "Mechanism",
            "size": {
              "width": 480,
              "height": 380
            },
            "showLabel": false,
            "data": {
              "title": "",
              "mechanism": "",
              "conditions": "",
              "steps": "",
              "failureModes": "",
              "documentation": ""
            },
            "ports": [
              {
                "id": "root",
                "label": "root",
                "direction": "bidirectional",
                "dataType": "any",
                "angle": 180
              }
            ]
          },
          "nodeDef": {
            "key": "topic-mechanism",
            "ref": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-mechanism.node-class.node",
            "source": "local",
            "version": ">=0.5.0",
            "defaults": {
              "label": "Mechanism",
              "size": {
                "width": 480,
                "height": 380
              },
              "showLabel": false,
              "data": {
                "title": "",
                "mechanism": "",
                "conditions": "",
                "steps": "",
                "failureModes": "",
                "documentation": ""
              },
              "ports": [
                {
                  "id": "root",
                  "label": "root",
                  "direction": "bidirectional",
                  "dataType": "any",
                  "angle": 180
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "views": [
            {
              "key": "topic-mechanism",
              "intent": "node",
              "payload": "node.web.detail",
              "ref": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-mechanism.node-class.node",
              "source": "local",
              "version": ">=0.2.0",
              "defaultPorts": []
            },
            {
              "key": "topic-mechanism",
              "intent": "node",
              "payload": "node.web.summary",
              "ref": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-mechanism.node-class.node",
              "source": "local",
              "version": ">=0.2.0",
              "defaultPorts": []
            },
            {
              "key": "topic-mechanism",
              "intent": "node",
              "payload": "node.web.icon",
              "ref": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-mechanism.node-class.node",
              "source": "local",
              "version": ">=0.2.0",
              "defaultPorts": []
            },
            {
              "key": "topic-mechanism",
              "intent": "editor",
              "payload": "editor.web",
              "ref": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-mechanism.node-class.node",
              "source": "local",
              "version": ">=0.2.0",
              "defaultPorts": []
            }
          ]
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "topic-template"
        },
        "steps": "1. Script text compiled via new Function('api', ...) inside the sandboxed iframe.\n2. Script calls an RPC method (getNodes, createNode, updateNode, createEdge, deleteNode, applyDeltas, ...) via postMessage.\n3. Host (usePluginRuntime.js handleScriptRequest) checks the per-run token and the run's remaining mutation budget.\n4. Host forwards the call to the real GraphCRUD mutation class, which is the same mutation surface the UI itself uses.\n5. Result (or error) is posted back to the sandboxed iframe.",
        "failureModes": "A run that exceeds the 15s timeout or the 200-RPC-call cap is presumably terminated/rejected (exact enforcement point not traced further); a script without allowMutations can call mutation RPCs but they run as dryRun and do not persist.",
        "documentation": "components/GraphEditor/Scripting/ScriptRunner.js, components/GraphEditor/hooks/usePluginRuntime.js, components/GraphEditor/Scripting/SCRIPTING.md (confirmed to match the code, not aspirational)."
      }
    },
